# What must never reach this repository, and why.
#
# This repo is private now and intended to go public later, so the window where
# a mistake is cheap is exactly now. .gitignore is only the first layer and the
# weakest: it is per-branch, and `git add -f` walks straight past it. The
# content checks live in tools/pre-commit.

# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# The real file stays local; app_secrets.h.example is committed with every
# value blanked. An example is never made by copying a working file.
app_secrets.h
arduino_secrets.h
secrets.h

# --- Which board this bench is allowed to flash ------------------------------
# A unique device ID is a device identifier in the same class as a MAC address.
# tools/bench.local.ps1.example is the committed template.
tools/bench.local.ps1

# --- Signing keys ------------------------------------------------------------
# The MCUboot signing key lives OUTSIDE every repository, in
# Documents/Arduino/mcuboot-signing/. These patterns are belt-and-braces for a
# key that gets generated into the tree by accident. Both halves of the
# key-file Kconfig fragment are local too: pmc-key.conf and mcuboot-key.conf
# name an absolute path on this machine, and their .example twins carry the
# fail-closed placeholder instead.
*.pem
*.key
*.priv
mcuboot/pmc-key.conf
app/mcuboot-key.conf

# --- Firmware images, BY EXTENSION rather than only by directory -------------
# `build/` is one `-d <dir>` away from not applying, and a firmware image
# contains, verbatim and in plaintext, every value that was #defined into it
# when it was built. A .map file additionally carries the builder's home
# directory on every line, and a .signed.bin carries the image header that
# names the signing key's hash.
*.bin
*.elf
*.map
*.hex
*.signed.bin
*.signed.hex

# --- Build trees -------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-*/
twister-out*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Captures and scratch ----------------------------------------------------
# RTT and boot logs are captured during a swap and routinely contain the board's
# own addresses. Keep them; do not commit them.
captures/
*.rtt
*.log
~$*

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   app/src/chan_table.inc     generated by tools/gen_channels.py
#   app/src/web_gen/*.h        generated by mkhtml.py
#   web/_hotspots.html         generated by tools/gen_channels.py
#   docs/CHANNELS.md           generated by tools/gen_channels.py
#
# Every one of those is generated AND committed, for two reasons. `--check`
# can only compare against a file in the tree, so ignoring them would quietly
# disable the drift guard that is the whole point of generating them. And a
# committed copy means the firmware builds on a machine with no Python.
